  "label": "Animal as Stereotype",
  "description": "The use of an animal (wild boar) to represent a human group or individual is a common trope in stereotyping and dehumanization. The wild boar is often associated with dirtiness, aggression, or 'wildness', which are used to justify negative attitudes toward people who are perceived as 'unrefined' or 'dangerous'.",
